{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"3a33af34e4d8a7902accddd8202823e2b0ce620ff5465512410b87271857e67b","digest":{"component_or_area":"mapping seam","key_entities":["[tool.rebar.mapping]","docs/config.md","docs/mapping-seam.md","docs/README.md","CHANGELOG",".bridge_state/projects.json","status","type","link","priority","create_defaults"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","portability","mapping seam","provider-neutral","migration safety","backward compatibility","config reference"],"propositions":["The mapping seam requires authoritative documentation covering the new config surface, echo-safe behaviors (breadcrumb, replay), and probe command across operators and future integrators.","The mapping seam must be provider-neutral with no capability whose only trigger is a specific CI provider, and must work across diverse or absent CI environments per plan-review portability criterion.","The feature is additive and backward-compatible: an absent [tool.rebar.mapping] section reproduces current hardcoded behavior exactly, with rollback achieved by deleting the section.","Every mapping behavior is exercised by injected-transport unit tests requiring no live Jira and no specific CI provider, with the only live touchpoint (probe) degrading to offline emit and never gating CI."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787524421544757001,"uuid":"afa4bff1-9ea9-47f4-9caa-2504e6de7dac"}